<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ashurbanipal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 669–627 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ashurbanipal was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a> from 669 to 627 BCE, the last great Assyrian ruler. He campaigned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> against the Kushite <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaohs</a>, destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/susa">Susa</a> and crushed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a>, and defeated a revolt by his brother in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>. He assembled a great library at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nineveh">Nineveh</a>, but the empire collapsed within a few decades of his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ashurbanipal.jpg" alt="Ashurbanipal" width="315" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: KeyolTranslater · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AshurbanipalKingOfAssyria.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
